{
  "borough": "Harrow",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed conversion of the dwellinghouse into three flats and the sub-division of the rear garden into three separate amenity areas, would result in an overly intensive use of the site and a poor standard of living accomodation, to the detriment of the living conditions of the potential future occupiers of the flats and the character and appearance of the property and the area, contrary to the National Planning Policy Framework (2023), policies D3 D (7) and (11) and D6 of The London Plan (2021), policies DM1, DM26 and DM27 of the Harrow Development Management Policies Local Plan (2013), the Mayor of London Supplementary Planning Guidance Housing (2016), and the adopted Supplementary Planning Document: Residential Design Guide (2010).&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed conversion of the dwellinghouse into three flats would result in an unacceptable vertical stacking arrangement between the ground floor bedroom of flat 2 and the kitchen/living/dinning room area of the first floor flat 3, to the detriment of the living conditions of the potential future occupiers of the flat 2, contrary to the high quality design aspirations of National Planning Policy Framework (2023), policies D3 D (7) and (11) and D6 of The London Plan (2021), policies DM1, and DM26 of the Harrow Development Management Policies Local Plan (2013), the Mayor of London Supplementary Planning Guidance Housing (2016), and the adopted Supplementary Planning Document: Residential Design Guide (2010).&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p style=&quot;margin: 0cm 0cm 0cm 36pt; line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;The\r\nproposed two storey side extension, by reason of its excessive depth would fail to provide a coherent pattern\r\nof development in the street scene thus would substantially harm the form,\r\nopenness and proportion of the site, relationship with the properties in the\r\nlocality accentuated by its prominent siting on a roundabout, to the detriment of the character\r\nand appearance of the streetscene and the pattern of development within the\r\nsurrounding area and would therefore be contrary to the high quality design\r\naspirations of the National Planning Policy Framework (2023), Policies D3.D(1)\r\nand D3.D(11) of The London Plan (2021), Policy CS.1B of the Harrow Core\r\nStrategy (2012), Policy DM1 of the Development Management Plan Local Policies\r\n(2013) and the Adopted Supplementary Planning Document: Residential Design\r\nGuide (2010).&lt;font face=&quot;Arial, sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
